clean_summary:
This was such a fun talk with Cat and Simon. If you missed it, I hope you get to check it out.

@aiDotEngineer: "This Year In Claude. Simon Willison chats with @catwu and @trq212 about the state of Claude AI, including Claude Code, Claude Fable, culture and product strategy at Anthropic, Claude Tag and multiplayer collaboration, the surprising success of Remote Control, HTML artifacts for code review, Auto Mode for long tasks, Claude for video editing, and how to be more ambitious as a developer by refusing to negotiate against oneself."

The discussion covers how coding agents have transformed workflows, the shift towards product sense over manual implementation, the benefits of modern rewrites, new collaboration tools like Claude Tag, the success of remote control features, evolving code review automation, building trust in model generations, optimizing for capability and user experience, safety and security practices, and fun, innovative projects built with Claude. It also includes a Q&A session with audience questions.
